# Machine-local overrides for the Muse-Glimmer-30B DUAL-card 262K + vision lane.
# MUST live in THIS directory — docker compose only auto-loads a .env from the directory
# it is invoked from, and serve.sh/switch.sh cd into the compose's own dir. A parent-level
# .env is silently never read (AGENTS.md).
#
# See long-vision.yml's header for the full rationale + the first-boot checklist.
# ⚠ THIS LANE HAS NEVER BOOTED. Values below are predictions.

MODEL_DIR=/home/pawl/models

# NOT pinned to one card — this lane is the whole point of having two.
# ⚠ Uses GPU0, so it CANNOT coexist with ComfyUI. When ComfyUI is running, boot the
# single-card sibling instead: ../../single/meta-kquant-17gb/dflash-vision.yml (131K).
DUAL_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1

# Layer split (NOT tensor-parallel — see the header on why -sm row would be wrong on this
# rig's PCIe x4 GPU1). Ratio form, like the deckard/hauhau dual lanes.
# Leans to GPU1 for two reasons: GPU0 carries the Windows desktop (~1.2 GiB), and llama.cpp
# pins the mmproj + draft model to the main GPU (0) on top of its layer share.
# ⚠ VERIFY on first boot from the load log ("CUDA0/CUDA1 buffer size" + "KV self size")
# and nvidia-smi on BOTH cards. If GPU0 is tight -> 0.8,1.2 ; if GPU1 is tight -> 1.0,1.0.
TENSOR_SPLIT=0.9,1.1

# Full 262K. Safe to use the plain name here: this directory has its own .env (the
# single-card dir needed LONG_CTX_SIZE only because two composes there share one .env).
# Requires the --override-kv pair in the compose — the GGUF declares 131072 and
# llama-server hard-caps the slot to n_ctx_train without it.
CTX_SIZE=262144
OVERRIDE_CTX=262144

# q8_0/q8_0 — kept for COMPARABILITY with both single-card lanes, not because f16 doesn't
# fit. f16 at 262K is 3.25 GiB (+1.52) and DOES fit here, unlike on one card. Flip both to
# f16 for max fidelity on a long agentic run, then re-measure prefill (a sibling thread
# measured q8_0 FASTER than f16: 609 vs 567 tok/s).
KV_TYPE_K=q8_0
KV_TYPE_V=q8_0

# Larger microbatch speeds prefill/TTFT on image tokens (up to 4096 visual tokens per
# image) + long text. MEASURED on this rig: 1024 beats 512 by ~4%, contra a community
# report. 512 hands back ~678 MiB if a card turns out tight.
UBATCH_SIZE=1024

# Effort lever for THIS model — a chat-template kwarg, NOT --reasoning (no <think> tags;
# reasoning rides an `assistant to=self` channel). Meta advises high/xhigh for coding +
# agentic work. MEASURED on the single-card lane: xhigh is a reproducible +2/20 on hard
# agentic follow-through and does NOTHING for simple tool dispatch — the setting is a
# CEILING, not a floor. Override per boot:
#   REASONING_STRENGTH=xhigh ./serve.sh muse-dual
REASONING_STRENGTH=high

# Block size is 16 = 1 anchor + 15 proposals; upstream clamps anything above 15.
# ⚠ BOOT-TIME ONLY on this build — per-request "speculative":{"n_max":N} is silently
# ignored, so changing depth means a reboot.
DFLASH_N_MAX=15

# Drafter switch, for A/B-ing DFlash without editing the compose:
#   draft-dflash = ON (default)   ·   none = OFF (frees 2.51 GiB)
# ⚠ The drafter COSTS prefill — measured -13.9% at 200K on the single long lane, needing a
# ~3.3K-token reply to break even. Flip to none for one short answer over a giant prompt.
SPEC_TYPE=draft-dflash

# LOCALLY BUILT image — no upstream one carries this architecture yet (llama.cpp PR #26841,
# commit 62bf73d, merged to master 2026-08-10). Built from master 030ebb5 with
# .devops/cuda.Dockerfile --target server, CUDA_DOCKER_ARCH=86 → 3090 ONLY.
# Swap to an official tag the moment one contains the commit:
#   git merge-base --is-ancestor 62bf73d25c53b8161f8a22894d4f90c4aebbd7d0 <tag>
LLAMACPP_IMAGE=club3090/llama.cpp:server-cuda-master-030ebb5-sm86

# Distinct name + port so it coexists with the single-card lanes in Hermes/LiteLLM (only
# one runs at a time under the GPU mutex, but all stay selectable).
#   8210 = single 131K + vision  ·  8211 = single 262K text  ·  8212 = THIS (dual 262K+vision)
SERVED_NAME=muse-glimmer-30b-dual
PORT=8212
